<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Dec-Feb.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in Dec-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to an average of 429,000 in Dec-Feb from 437,000 in Nov-Jan, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Dec-Feb 97   Nov-Jan 97   Dec-Feb 96</p>
<p> total number	  429,000	437,000	468,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force   6.4	    6.5	    7.0</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   Dec-Feb 97   Nov-Jan 97    Dec-Feb 96</p>
<p> total number	  417,000	429,000	457,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force   6.2	    6.4	    6.8</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated in relation to average 1996 labour force (6.681 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters had expected non-seasonally adjusted Dec-Feb unemployment of 438,000 and seasonally adjusted Dec-Feb unemployment of 427,000.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
